##* {{quote-book|en|year=1596|author=w:William Shakespeare; {{w|Thomas Kyd}} ''(uncertain)''|title=[[w:Edward III (play)|Edward III]]|section=act III, scene iv|url=https://archive.org/stream/cu31924013134337|passage={{...}} And now behold after my winters toyle, / My paynefull voyage on the boyſtrous ſea, / Of warres deuouring gulphes and ſteely rocks, / I bring my '''fraught''' vnto the wiſhed port / My Summers hope, my trauels ſweet reward {{...}}}}
