##* {{RQ:Gascoigne Flowres|title=Iocasta|act=V|scene=ii|page=148|passage=[O]ne the other fiercely did encounter, / Like Lions two '''yfraught''' with boyling wrath, {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Spenser Amoretti|sonnet=LXXVI|page=98|passage=Fayre boſome '''fraught''' vvith vertues richeſt treſure, / The [[nest|neaſt]] of loue, the lodging of delight: / the bovvre of bliſſe, the paradice of pleaſure, / the ſacred harbour of that heuenly ſpright.}}
##* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=a discourse '''fraught''' with all the commending excellences of speech}}
##* {{RQ:Young Centaur|page=367|passage=Liberty, '''fraught''' vvith bleſſings as it is, vvhen ''unabuſed'', has, perhaps been abuſed to our deſtruction.}}
