##* {{RQ:Macaulay Miscellaneous Writings|chapter=HC Speech 19 February 1844|page=658|passage=The government and the legislature, each in its own sphere, is deeply responsible for the continuance of a state of things which is '''fraught''' with danger to the State.}}
##* {{RQ:Isaac Taylor Ultimate Civilization|section=I|page=257|passage=He is a man of the meditative claſs:—he walks the ſtreets abſtractedly:—as he goes he digeſts enterpriſes, '''fraught''' with world-wide benefits.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=Rollo Ahmed|chapter=The Earliest Records of Black Magic|title=The Black Art|location=London|publisher=Senate, Studio Editions<!--Originally John Long-->|year=1936|year_published=1994|section=part I|page=22|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/soi-book-collection-3/kupdf.net_rollo-ahmed-the-black-art/page/n10/mode/1up|isbn=978-1-85958-048-6|passage=The simplest action was '''fraught''' with danger, and could only be accomplished with the aid of talismans and counter-spells, and people lived in constant dread of the unknown.}}
## {{lb|en|specifically}} Carrying or loaded with [[anxiety]], [[fear#Noun|fear]], or [[stress#Noun|stress]], for example, due to [[complexity]] or [[difficulty]]; [[distressed#Adjective|distressed]]; also, [[cause#Verb|causing]] [[distress#Noun|distress]]; [[distressing#Adjective|distressing]].
##: {{collocation|en|a '''fraught''' relationship&emsp;&emsp;&emsp; a '''fraught''' process}}
##* {{RQ:Telegraph|author=Oliver Brown|title=Oscar Pistorius jailed for five years&nbsp;– sport afforded no protection against his tragic fallibilities: Bladerunner's punishment for killing {{w|Reeva Steenkamp}} is but a frippery when set against the burden that her bereft parents, June and Barry, must carry [print version: No room for sentimentality in this tragedy, 13 September 2014, page&nbsp;S22]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231124221311/http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/oscar-pistorius/11089621/Oscar-Pistorius-jailed-for-five-years-sport-afforded-no-protection-against-his-tragic-fallibilities.html|section=Sport|date=21 October 2014|passage=But ever since the concept of "hamartia" recurred through {{w|Aristotle}}'s ''[[w:Poetics (Aristotle)|Poetics]]'', in an attempt to describe man's ingrained iniquity, our impulse has been to identify a telling defect in those brought suddenly and dramatically low. With [[w:Oscar Pistorius|[Oscar] Pistorius]], that task is '''fraught'''.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|author=Robin Leleux|title=A Royal Occasion as Heritage Projects Honoured: Sudbury Hill|journal=[[w:Rail (magazine)|Rail]]|location=Peterborough, Cambridgeshire|publisher=[[w:Bauer Media Group|Bauer Media]]|date=14 December 2022|issue=972|page=57|issn=0953-4563|oclc=999467860|passage=Installing lift shafts in station buildings which were not originally designed to accommodate them can be a '''fraught''' exercise, but a necessary one if the legitimate aspiration of the travelling public for step-free access is to be achieved. At Sudbury Hill, on London Underground's Piccadilly Line extension out to the north-western suburbs, Transport for London has achieved this with aplomb.}}
## ''Followed by'' '''with''': [[furnished#Adjective|furnished]], [[provided#Adjective|provided]].
##: {{synonyms|en|equipped|supplied}}
##* {{RQ:Marlorat Golding Revelation|chapter=2|verse=2|folio=32|passage=[W]hen the worlde is '''fraughted''' with ſo manye [[varlet]]tes, that it will be a long time ere a man ſhall diſcerne the faythful from the Hipocrites.|brackets=on}}
##* {{RQ:Spenser Fowre Hymnes|page=43|passage=Hovv vvondrouſly vvould he her face commend, / Aboue that Idole of his fayning thought, / That all the vvorld ſhold vvith his rimes be '''fraught'''?}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear Q1|act=I|scene=iv|sig=D|verso=1|page=34|passage=Come ſir, I vvould you vvould make vſe of that good vviſedome vvhereof I knovv you are '''fraught''', and put avvay theſe diſpoſitions, that of late tranſforme you from vvhat you rightly are.}}
##* {{RQ:Bacon Learning|book=1|folio=21|verso=1|folioend=22|folioref=22|passage=So, in naturall Hiſtorie, vvee ſee there hath not beene that choiſe and iudgement vſed, as ought to haue beene, as may appeare in the vvritings of ''[[w:Pliny the Elder|Plinius]]'', ''[[w:Gerolamo Cardano|Cardanus]]'', ''[[w:Albertus Magnus|Albertus]]'', and diuers of the Arabians, being '''fraught''' vvith much fabulous matter, a great part, not onely vntryed, but notoriouſly vntrue, to the great derogation of the credite of naturall Philoſophie, {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|lines=334–335|page=72|passage=Mules after theſe, Camels and Dromedaries, / And VVaggons '''fraught''' vvith Utenſils of vvar.}}
##* {{RQ:Swift Tale of a Tub|section=Discourse|sectionname=Sect[ion] II|page=307|passage=The firſt Ingredient, tovvards the Art of Canting, is a competent Share of ''Invvard Light'': that is to ſay, a large Memory, plentifully '''fraught''' vvith Theological Polyſyllables, and myſterious Texts from holy VVrit, applied and digeſted by thoſe Methods, and Mechanical Operations already related: {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Southey Thalaba|volume=I|pages=258–259|pageref=258|passage=The desert Pelican had built her nest / In that deep solitude. / And now returned from distant flight / '''Fraught''' with the river stream, / Her load of water had disburthened there. / Her young in the refreshing bath / Sported all wantonness; {{...}}}}

